{
  "$comment": "Treasury dataset contract, shared by the backend SQL (queries/governance/treasury_*.sql, wallet_*.sql, token_*.sql, holder_series.sql) and the UI parsers (model/treasuryRows.ts). Column ORDER is part of the contract. Dates are 'YYYY-MM-DD' strings; buckets are month starts 'YYYY-MM-01'. NULL means not measured / not priced, never 0. The live smoke test compares real result columns against this file.",
  "vocab": {
    "token_class": [
      "priced",
      "listed",
      "unverified",
      "spam",
      "retired_mirror"
    ],
    "spam_reason": [
      "",
      "impersonation",
      "lure",
      "obfuscated",
      "malformed",
      "mass_airdrop"
    ],
    "as_of_status": [
      "complete",
      "partial",
      "no_served_snapshot"
    ],
    "coverage_status": [
      "complete",
      "partial",
      "gap",
      "unpublished"
    ],
    "grain": [
      "chain",
      "wallet",
      "token"
    ],
    "price_source": [
      "hub",
      "hub_proxy",
      ""
    ],
    "asset_class": [
      "GNO",
      "ETH",
      "Stablecoins",
      "BTC",
      "RWA",
      "Other",
      ""
    ],
    "$comment": "price_source 'hub_proxy' = priced with a pegged asset's hub series (e.g. stETH with WETH, DAI with xDAI) — show as hub-priced with a 'peg proxy' marker. coverage_status: only 'gap' and 'unpublished' months are blanked (null) in charts; 'partial' months ARE drawn, with a note naming unserved_registry_symbols. spot_eligible = 1 only for token_class 'listed' (reviewed real tokens without a hub price) with known decimals; 'unverified' tokens are never spot-valued. treasury_token_detail may return ZERO rows when the treasury does not hold the token on the as-of day (history and price history can still exist)."
  },
